hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"242","Ahmad ibn Abdah told us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, informed us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “When he has done ablution from ritual impurity, he pours water from the vessel onto his right hand and pours it over it. He washes it, then He pours water on his left hand and washes his private part, and performs ablution as he performs prayer, then he inserts his palm into the vessel and says with his hand in his hair like this, He mixes it with his hand, until when he sees that the water has touched his skin, he pours the water on his head three times, and pours some into the vessel. upon him after he has finished.”"
